<title>BELGIUM: BOE's George says lira ERM deal tonight.</title>
<headline>BOE's George says lira ERM deal tonight.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of England governor Eddie George said on Sunday the European Union would decide tonight to allow the Italian lira back into the Exchange Rate Mechanism.</p>
<p>He said he felt the deal was close enough to allow him to leave a ministerial meeting on the issue in Brussels.  </p>
<p>&quot;There will be a decision tonight,&quot; George told reporters.</p>
<p>Asked if the decision was close, he said:</p>
<p>&quot;Close enough, so that is why I feel I can go home.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier the talks seemed deadlocked over the rate at which the lira should enter the currency grid, designed to offer stablity to member countries.</p>
<p>Italy wanted a weaker lira against the German mark, at least 1,000 lira per mark, while an EU majority was pushing for a stronger lira at between 950 and 980.</p>
</text>
